    {
      "id": "generics",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Lifetimes, generics, and type aliases\n\nGenerics let you write functions and types that work for many types.\nLifetimes are a special kind of generic that describe how references relate\nto each other. `type` aliases give a fresh name to an existing type.\n",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "generics-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "type Meters = f64;\nfn pick_first<'a>(items: &'a [i32]) -> &'a i32 {\n    &items[0]\n}\nfn identity<T>(value: T) -> T {\n    value\n}\n\nlet distance: Meters = 12.5;\nlet numbers = vec![7, 14, 21];\n\nreport(format!(\n    \"distance = {distance} m\\nidentity(3) = {}\\nfirst = {}\",\n    identity(3),\n    pick_first(&numbers)\n))",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 22,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "language = Rust\nyear = 2024\npi = 3.141592653589793\nis_fun = true\ninitial = M\n(12, 2, 35, 1, 2, 1.4, 1024)\ncounter = 5\nanswer = 42.5\ngreeting = Hello, Mars!\nshout = HELLO, MARS!\nwords = [\"Hello,\", \"Mars!\"]\ncharacters = 12\nreplaced = Hello, notebooks!\n21 C is mild: A jacket is enough\ncountdown = [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]\ndoubled = 10\npopped = [3, 2, 1]\nloop_count = 3\nsquare(9) = 81\naverage([2, 4, 6, 8]) = 5\npoint = (3, 4)\nx = 3, y = 4\narray = [10, 20, 30, 40]\nslice = [20, 30]\ntotal = 100\nprimes = [2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13]\nfirst = Some(2)\nlast = Some(13)\nmiddle = [3, 5, 7]\nnumbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\nsquares = [1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36]\nevens = [2, 4, 6]\nsum = 21\nproduct = 720\nmax = Some(6)\n[(\"be\", 2), (\"not\", 1), (\"or\", 1), (\"to\", 2)]\nrectangle = Rectangle { width: 3.0, height: 4.0 }\narea = 12\nperimeter = 14\ncircle = 12.57\nrectangle = 12.00\ngood = Ok(42)\nbad = Err(\"`forty-two` is not a number\")\nfirst_even = Some(2)\nfallback = -1\nparsed = parsed 42\ncategory = pass\noffset = 10\nvalues = [1, 2, 3, 4]\nadjusted = [11, 12, 13, 14]\nMAX_POINTS = 100\nNEXT_ID = 1\nstatic_ref = 1\ntotal = 100\nreference = 100\ncounter = 6\nmath::double(21) = 42\nhello, Mars\norigin = Point2D { x: 0, y: 0 }\norigin == other: true\ndistance = 12.5 m\nidentity(3) = 3\nfirst = 7\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "traits",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Traits\n\nA `trait` defines shared behavior that many types can implement. Trait\nobjects (`&dyn Trait`) let you work with several different types through one\ncommon interface.\n",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "traits-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "trait Describe {\n    fn describe(&self) -> String;\n}\n\nimpl Describe for i32 {\n    fn describe(&self) -> String {\n        format!(\"integer {self}\")\n    }\n}\n\nlet number = 42;\n\nreport(number.describe())",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 23,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "language = Rust\nyear = 2024\npi = 3.141592653589793\nis_fun = true\ninitial = M\n(12, 2, 35, 1, 2, 1.4, 1024)\ncounter = 5\nanswer = 42.5\ngreeting = Hello, Mars!\nshout = HELLO, MARS!\nwords = [\"Hello,\", \"Mars!\"]\ncharacters = 12\nreplaced = Hello, notebooks!\n21 C is mild: A jacket is enough\ncountdown = [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]\ndoubled = 10\npopped = [3, 2, 1]\nloop_count = 3\nsquare(9) = 81\naverage([2, 4, 6, 8]) = 5\npoint = (3, 4)\nx = 3, y = 4\narray = [10, 20, 30, 40]\nslice = [20, 30]\ntotal = 100\nprimes = [2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13]\nfirst = Some(2)\nlast = Some(13)\nmiddle = [3, 5, 7]\nnumbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\nsquares = [1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36]\nevens = [2, 4, 6]\nsum = 21\nproduct = 720\nmax = Some(6)\n[(\"be\", 2), (\"not\", 1), (\"or\", 1), (\"to\", 2)]\nrectangle = Rectangle { width: 3.0, height: 4.0 }\narea = 12\nperimeter = 14\ncircle = 12.57\nrectangle = 12.00\ngood = Ok(42)\nbad = Err(\"`forty-two` is not a number\")\nfirst_even = Some(2)\nfallback = -1\nparsed = parsed 42\ncategory = pass\noffset = 10\nvalues = [1, 2, 3, 4]\nadjusted = [11, 12, 13, 14]\nMAX_POINTS = 100\nNEXT_ID = 1\nstatic_ref = 1\ntotal = 100\nreference = 100\ncounter = 6\nmath::double(21) = 42\nhello, Mars\norigin = Point2D { x: 0, y: 0 }\norigin == other: true\ndistance = 12.5 m\nidentity(3) = 3\nfirst = 7\ninteger 42\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "statistics",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Summary statistics\n\nThe next cell computes count, total, mean, minimum, maximum, and median for a\nsmall list of integers. This is the data-analysis example merged into the tour.\n",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "statistics-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "let values = vec![3_i32, 7, 4, 9, 12, 6];\nlet total: i32 = values.iter().sum();\nlet mean = total as f64 / values.len() as f64;\nlet minimum = values.iter().min().copied();\nlet maximum = values.iter().max().copied();\n\nlet mut sorted = values.clone();\nsorted.sort();\nlet median = if sorted.len() % 2 == 0 {\n    let middle = sorted.len() / 2;\n    (sorted[middle - 1] + sorted[middle]) as f64 / 2.0\n} else {\n    sorted[sorted.len() / 2] as f64\n};\n\nreport(format!(\n    \"values = {values:?}\\ncount = {}\\ntotal = {total}\\nmean = {mean}\\nmin = {minimum:?}\\nmax = {maximum:?}\\nmedian = {median}\",\n    values.len()\n))",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 24,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "text",
